distributed revision control system with an unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full access to internals. Prior to 2.50.2, 2.51.3, 2.52.1, 2.53.1, 2.54.1, 2.55.1, and 2.56.1, an attacker-controlled repository hosted by the attacker rather than on a normal forge site can exploit git clone --recurse-submodules by causing Git to overwrite a submodule gitfile with a symbolic link. The symbolic link can point to a directory containing attacker-controlled Git configuration or hooks, allowing those hooks or configuration to execute code on the cloning user's system. The issue requires the recursive-submodule option, and users should avoid cloning repositories from untrusted sources. This issue is fixed in versions 2.50.2, 2.51.3, 2.52.1, 2.53.1, 2.54.1, 2.55.1, and 2.56.1.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Git: Recursive clones are susceptible to Remote Code Execution","topics":["advisory","cwe-59"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-17T07:01:31.693825Z","vendors":[]}],"meta":{"cve_inputs":["CVE-2026-128038","CVE-2026-107904","CVE-2026-111973","CVE-2026-97639","CVE-2026-97187","CVE-2026-97043","CVE-2026-97038","CVE-2026-97037","CVE-2026-97036","CVE-2026-97035","CVE-2026-97034","CVE-2026-97033","CVE-2026-85778","CVE-2026-82156","CVE-2026-21176","CVE-2026-21175","CVE-2026-21153","CVE-2026-21152","CVE-2026-21151","CVE-2026-18491","CVE-2026-18241","CVE-2026-16609","CVE-2026-16545","CVE-2026-129321","CVE-2026-129253","CVE-2026-129252","CVE-2026-128849","CVE-2026-126982","CVE-2026-126526","CVE-2026-126325","CVE-2026-126141","CVE-2026-125920","CVE-2026-124737","CVE-2026-124223","CVE-2026-124222","CVE-2026-123142","CVE-2026-122226","CVE-2026-122045","CVE-2026-121948","CVE-2026-121684","CVE-2026-121533","CVE-2026-120869","CVE-2026-120868","CVE-2026-120387","CVE-2026-11768","CVE-2026-118961","CVE-2026-115736","CVE-2026-115428","CVE-2026-115219","CVE-2026-115218","CVE-2026-114560","CVE-2026-112203","CVE-2026-111760","CVE-2026-111747","CVE-2026-1109